  "word_count_target": 140,
  "story_en": "Paul leaves the shop and walks toward a public park. In the center of the green space, he finds an empty wooden bench near a fountain. The weather is pleasant, and birds sing in the tall trees.\n\nHe sits down, unrolls his paper map, and begins to study the lines. He marks his current position near the town square with a pencil. Then, he looks for the main train station.\n\n“The station is three miles north,” Paul notes quietly. “I should follow this wide avenue and cross the bridge over the river.”\n\nA young woman walking her dog passes by and notices the map. “Are you planning a long trip?” she asks with interest.\n\n“Yes, I am going to the mountains,” Paul explains.\n\n“Take the morning train,” she suggests kindly. “It is fast and safe.”\n\nPaul thanks her for the advice, folds the map, and prepares to walk.",
